- ### Values that cross the boundary
+ ### Valores que cruzan la frontera

- A Scala value is passed as an argument only where an `Interoperable` instance says which
- foreign type it corresponds to:
+ Un valor de Scala solo se pasa como argumento donde una instancia de `Interoperable` indica a qué
+ tipo foráneo corresponde:

= foreign type it corresponds to:
=
- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Scala type
- column  WebIDL type
+ column  Tipo de Scala
+ column  Tipo de WebIDL

- row  `Text`  `DOMString`, `USVString`, `ByteString`, `CSSOMString`
+ row  `Text`  `DOMString`, `USVString`, `ByteString`, `CSSOMString`

- row  `Boolean`  `boolean`
+ row  `Boolean`  `boolean`

- row  `S8`  `byte`
+ row  `S8`  `byte`

- row  `U8`  `octet`
+ row  `U8`  `octet`

- row  `S16`  `short`
+ row  `S16`  `short`

- row  `U16`  `unsigned short`
+ row  `U16`  `unsigned short`

- row  `S32`  `long`
+ row  `S32`  `long`

- row  `U32`  `unsigned long`
+ row  `U32`  `unsigned long`

- row  `S64`  `long long`
+ row  `S64`  `long long`

- row  `U64`  `unsigned long long`
+ row  `U64`  `unsigned long long`

- row  `F32`  `float`, `unrestricted float`
+ row  `F32`  `float`, `unrestricted float`

- row  `F64`  `double`, `unrestricted double`
+ row  `F64`  `double`, `unrestricted double`

- row  `List[T]`  `sequence<T>`, `FrozenArray<T>`
+ row  `List[T]`  `sequence<T>`, `FrozenArray<T>`

- row  `Map[K, V]`  `record<K, V>`
+ row  `Map[K, V]`  `record<K, V>`

- row  `Optional[T]`  `T?`, with `Unset` as `null`
+ row  `Optional[T]`  `T?`, con `Unset` como `null`

= row  `Optional[T]`  `T?`, with `Unset` as `null`
- ```
+ ```

- The numbers are [sized](numbers.md#numeric-types), so a parameter which is declared `long`
- takes an `S32`, and not an unsized `Int`:
+ Los números tienen [tamaño](numbers.md#numeric-types), así que un parámetro declarado como `long`
+ recibe un `S32`, y no un `Int` sin tamaño:

= takes an `S32`, and not an unsized `Int`:
=
- ```scala
+ ```scala

- val left: S32 = 0
+ val left: S32 = 0

- val top: S32 = 480
+ val top: S32 = 480

- val scrolled = window.scrollTo(left, top)
+ val scrolled = window.scrollTo(left, top)

= val scrolled = window.scrollTo(left, top)
- ```
+ ```

- Each argument is checked against the declared type of its parameter, in the foreign type
- system's own terms. `scrollTo` wants two values of the foreign type `s32`, and an `S32` is
- the Scala value which provides one.
+ Cada argumento se comprueba contra el tipo declarado de su parámetro, en los términos del propio
+ sistema de tipos foráneo. `scrollTo` quiere dos valores del tipo foráneo `s32`, y un `S32` es el
+ valor de Scala que proporciona uno.

- ### Serializing to JavaScript
+ ### Serializar a JavaScript

- A foreign value's `expr` is its expression, a `Foreign.Expression`, which is a small tree of
- these nodes:
+ El `expr` de un valor foráneo es su expresión, un `Foreign.Expression`, que es un pequeño árbol de
+ estos nodos:

= these nodes:
=
- ```tabular
+ ```tabular

- column  Node
- column  Stands for
- column  Renders as
- row  `Reference(name)`  a global  `document`
- row  `Select(target, member, owner)`  a member of a value  `target.member`
- row  `Apply(target, arguments)`  a call  `target(arguments)`
- row  `Index(target, index)`  an index access  `target[index]`
- row  `Literal(value)`  a constant  `'text'`, `42`
+ column  Nodo
+ column  Representa
+ column  Se escribe como
+ row  `Reference(name)`  una variable global  `document`
+ row  `Select(target, member, owner)`  un miembro de un valor  `target.member`
+ row  `Apply(target, arguments)`  una llamada  `target(arguments)`
+ row  `Index(target, index)`  un acceso por índice  `target[index]`
+ row  `Literal(value)`  una constante  `'text'`, `42`

= row  `Literal(value)`  a constant  `'text'`, `42`
- ```
+ ```

- `Javascript.serialize` writes the tree as JavaScript source text:
+ `Javascript.serialize` escribe el árbol como texto fuente JavaScript:

= `Javascript.serialize` writes the tree as JavaScript source text:
=
- ```scala fuel
+ ```scala fuel

= `Javascript.serialize` writes the tree as JavaScript source text:
=
= ```scala fuel
- run
